---
qmd:
  collection: slipbox
  search_mode: query

clustering:
  method: average-linkage
  # Average-linkage cosine cutoff; higher = tighter/more clusters.
  # ~0.64 suits embeddinggemma book prose.
  threshold: 0.64
  min_cluster_size: 1

notes:
  id_style: timestamp
  link_style: wikilink
  frontmatter: yaml
---

# House style

- Write each literature note as a **single atomic idea**, restated in your own
  words — never a quote dump. If it needs two ideas, make two notes.
- Keep notes short and self-contained: a reader should understand the idea
  without opening the source.
- Title each note as a full sentence that states the idea (e.g. "Retrieval
  practice strengthens memory more than rereading").
- Tag with lowercase, hyphenated topics.
- Always link a note back to its source reference, and to related notes when you
  see a connection.
